The Section-118 carrier coefficient, older scalar floors, and the historical \(R_F=o(D)\) outer-pocket synthesis are not the live bottleneck. Audit.52 already eliminates \(R_F=o(D)\).

Do not infer a source competitor merely from reciprocal \((2,3)\)-sparsity, many return paths, positive physical residual, or a weighted stress-energy decrease.

## Exact next split

### Full-core branch

A sufficiently large survivor now carries all of the following simultaneously:

- strict scalar surplus above \(\mu_{\rm hull}\);
- linear fixed-boundary residual;
- \(\sigma_C=0\) and a smooth exact contact manifold;
- a positive reciprocal \((2,3)\)-sparse internal train graph;
- at least \(q-k\) outer-ended trains;
- globally vertex-disjoint actual loaded-return capacity indexed by exceptional-face defect;
- a joint bulk/face endpoint bank of size at least \(\pi D/4+Q/4-o(D)\) whenever the quadratic unloaded-rhombus bulk is selected.

The terminal geometry also has a forced alternative. Along a subsequence with \(q/D\to\pi\):

- if \(u_B=o(D)\), every outer-ended train family is second-depletable and a linear physical unit-wall residual bank exists;
- if also \(x_B=o(D)\), then
  \[
  e_{BI}+6(Q-f)
  \ge
  sD+2k+\frac{S_U}{2}-o(D).
  \]

Therefore do **not** spend the run on another small-residual theorem, another return-count Hall argument, another proof that internal train columns are sparse, or another outer-train depletion theorem in this scope.

The live theorem is active-diameter feasibility. High-value routes are:

1. use the exact contact manifold and positive reciprocal train graph to parameterize a finite family of contact-preserving directions whose active-diameter derivatives can be controlled simultaneously;
2. use the globally disjoint loaded-return paths as dual certificates or independent boundary controls for those contact-manifold directions;
3. in the terminal short-pocket branch, spend the pairwise wall-disjoint physical frustration bank collectively rather than seeking a single-wall refill;
4. combine the joint bulk/face separator bank with the Sections 122--123 global detour/payment currency to force more active-diameter controls than the diameter cage can support;
5. prove that failure of all such simultaneous directions forces an exact unit equilateral triangle.

A successful source competitor must check the finite maximum over **every** active diameter pair and preserve every lower separation. A weighted average decrease is not enough.

### Macroscopic inactive-container branch

This remains separate and open. The missing theorem must force an exact unit triangle, alter/replace part of the old diameter-carrying core, or construct a same-cardinality feasible source with strictly smaller global diameter.

